{"raw": {"https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-biology-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology", "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges 9 Month Faculty Opening at: Oct 16 2026 - 14:00 CDT VP Area: Arts & Sciences Department: Arts & Sciences FLSA Status: Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health profession related programs. While area of specialization is open, candidates will be expected to teach Human Anatomy and Human Physiology. Additional courses may include Introductory Biology for Majors, Microbiology, and/or Immunology or other courses to complement the pre-health profession related curriculum. The search committee is especially interested in candidates who, through their teaching, scholarship, and/or service, will contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community. The Department of Biology is interested in candidates who understand the barriers facing different groups of students and are passionate about helping all students meet their academic and career goals. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled, with a start date of August 2027. Finalists will be expected to present an engaging teaching demonstration as part of the interview process. Qualifications A PhD in biological sciences and previous college teaching experience is preferred, while ABD candidates will be considered. Compensation, rank, and length of tenure track will be commensurate with experience. Duties Duties of this position include teaching 21 credit hours annually, active participation in departmental, college, and university service, establishing an active research program involving undergraduates, active participation in the department's assessment program, participation in student recruiting and retention efforts for the college and the university. Procedure for Submitting Applications Submit a 1) cover letter with a brief statement of teaching philosophy and research interests 2) curriculum vitae containing list of professional references, and 3) unofficial transcripts. Contact For Additional Questions Search Chair: Dr. Nikki Seagraves nseagraves@okcu.edu Diversity Advocate: Dr. Stephen Prilliman sgprilliman@oku.edu About the Department of Biology Biology students enjoy small class sizes taught by Ph.D. faculty that also guide students through one of four curricular paths (Biology, Biology Education, Biology-Pre-Allied Health, and Biology-Pre-Med) and through preparation for graduate school and professional programs or employment after graduation. See department website for more information: https://www.okcu.edu/programs/biology . About the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University The Petree College of Arts and Sciences embraces the value of a liberal arts education and prepares students in all disciplines to think critically, creatively, and ethically. Our students are challenged to become servant leaders through an education that engages them to become socially and ecologically responsible citizens in our world. Through rigorous coursework taught by excellent faculty, Petree College is committed to an education that is relevant, socially engaged, and life transforming. The faculty and staff of Petree College are not only concerned about preparing students for careers. More importantly, we want to prepare you for life. We hope that you will join us to participate in an education that will make a difference for you and for the world. About Oklahoma City University Oklahoma City University was founded in 1904 and is a coeducational, urban, private university located in the Uptown district of Oklahoma City. The university is affiliated with the United Methodist Church and offers a wide variety of degrees in the liberal arts and sciences disciplines. Oklahoma City University is the only Oklahoma institution listed in the top tier of the regional, master's-level university category by U.S. News and World Report magazine. Employee Benefits The faculty of OCU are afforded a comprehensive benefits package designed to fit the needs of you and your family. Benefits offered include: health (medical, dental and vision) insurance, flexible spending accounts, university paid life insurance, university paid long-term disability insurance, retirement plans, and tuition remission for employees and qualifying dependents who wish to take classes or pursue a degree at OCU. Apply Now! Content missing Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Arts & Sciences The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health profession related programs. While area of specialization is open, candidates will be expected to teach Human Anatomy and Human Physiology. Additional courses may include Introductory Biology for Majors, Microbiology, and/or Immunology or other courses to complement the pre-health profession related curriculum. NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment Dance and Entertainment School Oklahoma City University invites applications for the nine-month, non-tenure track full-time faculty position of Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment beginning in January 2027 or August 2027. Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor) PA Program Oklahoma City University invites applications for the position of Principal Faculty, Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor in the Physician Assistant (PA) Program. This is a full-time, 12-month non-tenure track position located in the heart of Oklahoma City. The successful candidate will contribute to the education and development of future healthcare professionals and play a pivotal role in advancing the mission of the PA program. Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time or half-time adult-gerontology acute care nurse practitioner (AGACNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month or 12-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Administrative Assistant II Law School The Administrative Assistant II serves as the main point of contact for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the Law School by creating positive first and last impressions, as well as supporting the Law Dean's Office and law school departments. The Administrative Assistant II will work and communicate effectively with the judiciary, donors, alumni, attorneys, faculty, staff, students, vendors, and general public. While maintaining a pleasant and professional demeanor, this position will work with diverse, frequently changing priorities and situations. The Administrative Assistant II will demonstrate confidentiality, reliability, discretion, accuracy, and a strong service orientation. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) df161e32 Last Name (required) 4ee8990d Email (required) a4a8b007 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details \u00d7 This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"}, "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/np-clinical-instructor-or-assistant-professor-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {"title": "NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor", "description": "NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges 9 Month Faculty Opening at: Oct 15 2026 - 15:00 CDT VP Area: Nursing School Department: Nursing School FLSA Status: Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. The faculty member will: Prepare and conduct courses in conformity with outcomes of the university, Kramer School of Nursing, and approving accrediting agencies Evaluate student learning, skills, and abilities; and maintain records of such evaluations Engagement in scholarship that supports Kramer School of Nursing\u2019s mission Serve the University and the Kramer School of Nursing, including committee work as appropriate Participate in professional organizations as a member Adhere to all policies within the Oklahoma City University Faculty Handbook, KSN Employee Handbook, the OCU Student Handbook, and the KSN Student Handbook Participation in the OCU assessment program, and in student recruiting and retention efforts for KSN and the university Other duties as assigned. Education and Experience: Education: Terminal degree preferred Oklahoma RN with APRN recognition required MSN or DNP degree, Psychiatric Mental Health NP certification required Preference will be given to candidates who hold dual national certification as a nurse practitioner, including PMHNP certification Experience: Evidence of current practice with a minimum of two years full-time equivalent practice as a Registered Nurse in a clinical setting preceding the first date of first employment as a teacher.* Two (2) years of advanced practice nursing experience required. Both clinical and teaching experience are preferred, but related professional credentials will be considered. *per requirements of the Oklahoma Nursing Practice Act and Rules and Regulations of said Act. (1994) Additional Qualifications: Valid license to practice as a registered nurse and nurse practitioner in Oklahoma National certification as a psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner Kramer School of Nursing: Established in 1981, Kramer School of Nursing is now the premier private nursing school in the seven-state region in all quality measures. The School is committed to providing educational and service opportunities that prepare professional nurses who practice with integrity, knowledge, and compassion. In addition to the pre-licensure baccalaureate program offered in part-time, full-time, and accelerated options to first and second bachelor\u2019s degree students, Kramer also offers the RN-to-BSN (both on campus and in rural areas), the Master of Science in Nursing, the Doctor of Nursing Practice (including the Family Nurse Practitioner, Adult Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, and Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner). The University: Oklahoma City University was founded in 1904 and is a coeducational, urban, private university located in the Uptown district of Oklahoma City. The university is affiliated with the United Methodist Church and offers a wide variety of degrees in the liberal arts and sciences disciplines. Oklahoma City University is the only Oklahoma institution listed in the top tier of the regional, master's-level university category by U.S. News and World Report magazine. Employee Benefits The faculty of OCU are afforded a comprehensive benefits package designed to fit the needs of you and your family. Benefits offered include: health (medical, dental and vision) insurance, flexible spending accounts, university paid life insurance, university paid long-term disability insurance, retirement plans, and tuition remission for employees and qualifying dependents who wish to take classes or pursue a degree at OCU. Required Application Materials All applications submitted must include: CV and Cover Letter with Professional References listed Statement of Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c192ab77 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Subm