-time, 12-month non-tenure track position located in the heart of Oklahoma City. The successful candidate will contribute to the education and development of future healthcare professionals and play a pivotal role in advancing the mission of the PA program. Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time or half-time adult-gerontology acute care nurse practitioner (AGACNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month or 12-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Administrative Assistant II Law School The Administrative Assistant II serves as the main point of contact for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the Law School by creating positive first and last impressions, as well as supporting the Law Dean's Office and law school departments. The Administrative Assistant II will work and communicate effectively with the judiciary, donors, alumni, attorneys, faculty, staff, students, vendors, and general public. While maintaining a pleasant and professional demeanor, this position will work with diverse, frequently changing priorities and situations. The Administrative Assistant II will demonstrate confidentiality, reliability, discretion, accuracy, and a strong service orientation. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) f54d6e7d Last Name (required) 8f9209d4 Email (required) da8bee78 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details \u00d7 This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/principal-faculty-physician-assistant-program-assistant-or-associate-clinical-professor-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {"title": "Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor)", "description": "Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor) - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor) - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor) Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges 12 Month Faculty Opening at: Aug 20 2026 - 09:00 CDT VP Area: PA Program Department: PA Program FLSA Status: Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: Oklahoma City University invites applications for the position of Principal Faculty, Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor in the Physician Assistant (PA) Program. This is a full-time, 12-month non-tenure track position located in the heart of Oklahoma City. The successful candidate will contribute to the education and development of future healthcare professionals and play a pivotal role in advancing the mission of the PA program. Responsibilities: Provide didactic education and course coordination for first-year PA students. Facilitate small group learning experiences and provide clinical instruction. Offer academic counseling and support to students on academic issues. Collaborate with program faculty and staff in curriculum development and assessment. Participate in the development and maintenance of clinical rotation sites. Serve as a mentor and advisor to PA students. Engage in scholarly activities and professional development. Contribute to university and program committees as assigned. Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree with eligibility for licensure as a Physician Assistant in Oklahoma. Current certification by the NCCPA and eligibility for licensure in Oklahoma. Experience in graduate-level education preferred, including syllabi, test, and lecture preparation. Ability to work autonomously in providing direct patient care services. Minimum of two years of experience in PA education and providing direct patient care services preferred. About the PA Program: The Physician Assistant Program at Oklahoma City University is dedicated to preparing competent and compassionate healthcare professionals to meet the growing needs of our community. With a focus on excellence in education, clinical practice, and service, our program aims to address healthcare disparities and improve health outcomes across Oklahoma. About Oklahoma City University: Founded in 1904, Oklahoma City University is a leading private institution located in the vibrant Uptown district of Oklahoma City. Recognized for its commitment to academic excellence and community engagement, OCU is proud to be a top-tier university in the region. The university offers a diverse range of health profession program within the College of Health Professions that includes the Physician Assistant program, Physical Therapy program, and Nursing programs. Application Process: To apply, please visit the OCU Careers website and submit the following materials: Cover letter outlining your qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae detailing your education, experience, and scholarly achievements. Copy of unofficial transcripts. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For inquiries about the position or the application process, please contact the search Chair, Bobby Bosse, at rbosse@okcu.edu. Oklahoma City University is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity in the workplace. We encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e0b4db4c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments PA Program PA Program Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) ca69a536 Last Name (required) 7adabdbf Email (required) 9786f35c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Arts & Sciences The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health profession related programs. While area of specialization is open, candidates will be expected to teach Human Anatomy and Human Physiology. Additional courses may include Introductory Biology for Majors, Microbiology, and/or Immunology or other courses to complement the pre-health profession related curriculum. NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment Dance and Entertainment School Oklahoma City University invites applications for the nine-month, non-tenure track full-tim