luations Engagement in scholarship that supports Kramer School of Nursing\u2019s mission Serve the University and the Kramer School of Nursing, including committee work as appropriate Participate in professional organizations as a member Adhere to all policies within the Oklahoma City University Faculty Handbook, KSN Employee Handbook, the OCU Student Handbook, and the KSN Student Handbook Participation in the OCU assessment program, and in student recruiting and retention efforts for KSN and the university Other duties as assigned. Education and Experience: Education: Terminal degree preferred Oklahoma RN with APRN recognition required MSN or DNP degree, Adult Gero Acute Care NP certification required Preference will be given to candidates who hold dual national certification as a nurse practitioner, including AGACNP certification Experience: Evidence of current practice with a minimum of two years full-time equivalent practice as a Registered Nurse in a clinical setting preceding the first date of first employment as a teacher.* Two (2) years of advanced practice nursing experience required. Both clinical and teaching experience are preferred, but related professional credentials will be considered. *per requirements of the Oklahoma Nursing Practice Act and Rules and Regulations of said Act. (1994) Additional Qualifications: Valid license to practice as a registered nurse and nurse practitioner in Oklahoma National certification as an adult-gerontology acute care nurse practitioner Kramer School of Nursing: Established in 1981, Kramer School of Nursing is now the premier private nursing school in the seven-state region in all quality measures. The School is committed to providing educational and service opportunities that prepare professional nurses who practice with integrity, knowledge, and compassion. In addition to the pre-licensure baccalaureate program offered in part-time, full-time, and accelerated options to first and second bachelor\u2019s degree students, Kramer also offers the RN-to-BSN (both on campus and in rural areas), the Master of Science in Nursing, the Doctor of Nursing Practice (including the Family Nurse Practitioner, Adult Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, and Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner). The University: Oklahoma City University was founded in 1904 and is a coeducational, urban, private university located in the Uptown district of Oklahoma City. The university is affiliated with the United Methodist Church and offers a wide variety of degrees in the liberal arts and sciences disciplines. Oklahoma City University is the only Oklahoma institution listed in the top tier of the regional, master's-level university category by U.S. News and World Report magazine. Required Application Materials All applications submitted must include: CV and Cover Letter with Professional References listed Statement of Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 5833d490 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Nursing School Nursing School Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) 96a30d28 Last Name (required) 45156452 Email (required) c70c34b3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Arts & Sciences The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health profession related programs. While area of specialization is open, candidates will be expected to teach Human Anatomy and Human Physiology. Additional courses may include Introductory Biology for Majors, Microbiology, and/or Immunology or other courses to complement the pre-health profession related curriculum. NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment Dance and Entertainment School Oklahoma City University invites applications for the nine-month, non-tenure track full-time faculty position of Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment beginning in January 2027 or August 2027. Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor) PA Program Oklahoma City University invites applications for the position of Principal Faculty, Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor in the Physician Assistant (PA) Program. This is a full-time, 12-month non-tenure track position located in the heart of Oklahoma City. The successful candidate will contribute to the education and development of future healthcare professionals and play a pivotal role in advancing the mission of the PA program. Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time or half-time adult-gerontology acute care nurse practitioner (AGACNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month or 12-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Administrative Assistant II Law School The Administrative Assistant II serves as the main point of contact for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the Law School by creating positive first and last impressions, as well as supporting the Law Dean's Office and law school departments. The Administrative Assistant II will work and communicate effectively with the judiciary, donors, alumni, attorneys, faculty, staff, students, vendors, and general public. While maintaining a pleasant and professional demeanor, this position will work with diverse, frequently changing priorities and situations. The Administrative Assistant II will demonstrate confidentiality, reliability, discretion, accuracy, and a strong service orientation. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 856e6a1d Last Name (required) a4c6db7e Email (required) 9e786c04 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details \u00d7 This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/administrative-assistant-ii-law-school-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {"title": "Administrative Assistant II", "description": "Administrative Assistant II - Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Administrative Assistant II - Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Administrative Assistant II Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges Regular Full-Time Staff Opening at: Oct 5 2026 - 14:00 CDT VP Area: Law School Department: Law School FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: The Administrative Assistant II serves as the main point of contact for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the Law School by creating positive first and last impressions, as well as supporting the Law Dean's Office and law school departments. The Administrative Assistant II will work and communicate effectively with the judiciary, donors, alumni, attorneys, faculty, staff, students, vendors, and general public. While maintaining a pleasant and professional demeanor, this position will work with diverse, frequently changing priorities and situations. The Administrative Assistant II will demonstrate confidentiality, reliability, discretion, accuracy, and a strong service orientation. Required Minimum Education: A high school diploma or equivalent is required. Preferred Education: A bachelor's degree in business or related field is preferred. Minimum Qualifications: Two years of administrative support experience is required including accepted office organization, accounting, written and oral communication practices, and customer service Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education or legal environment is preferred. Job Duties: 100% - Law School/Harvey Building Support: \u2022 Serves as the first point of contact at the School of Law Harvey Building main/security entry, providing administrative support to process faculty, students, staff, guests, visitors, and vendors utilizing established identification and data collection and storage procedures to permit access to the building interior through the security turnstiles. Monitors and provides instructions on use of turnstiles and fob/card entry and notifies the appropriate parties with system problems. \u2022 Contacts administrators, faculty and staff when guests or visitors arrive. Answers main School of Law phone number. Provides assistance to faculty, staff, students, guests and visitors with law school, building, parking and service inquiries directing them to the appropriate departments as required. Knows law school functions, departments, personnel and procedures and has familiarity of other functions and departments within the University. \u2022 Receives routine and emergency procedure and notification training from and interacts with the OCU Police Department. Monitors security cameras as required. \u2022 Using specialized event management software, assists with logistical coordination of the Harvey Building by processing academic and non-academic requests for space and visitor parking. Adds and configures web users and groups. Enters, confirms and maintains room and parking reservations for academic classes, special events, student meetings, etc. Generates reports as required. \u2022 Assists Law Dean's Office with building management and maintenance issues by collecting complaints and notifications and submitting work orders on web-based system, monitoring completion of work orders. Notifies vending machine companies of needed repair or supply issues. \u2022 Serves as central location for USPS incoming/outgoing mail, overnight mail and other special deliveries for the Harvey Building. Main contact for service entry phone and, after reviewing camera display, allows vendor or delivery service to enter building. Administrative Services support: \u2022 Supports Executive Assistant by collecting and reviewing forms, receipts and other backup materials for reimbursements and invoices. Cross trains with Executive Assistant to insure appropriate backup. \u2022 Utilizing Access database integrates data from purchasing card website and creates, distributes and collects monthly law school purchasing card reports, confirming accurate completion. \u2022 Deals with confidential information or issues concerning budget, students, alumni or operations, referring matter to appropriate administrator. \u2022 Composes routine and general correspondence in accordance with established office procedures and policies. Shares in performance of general office tasks as coordinated and delegated by the Executive Assistant. \u2022 Assists in creation and maintenance of electronic and traditional files utilizing appropriate share drives as required. Remains current on all software and equipment required by position. \u2022 Creates and/or changes position desk manual, forms and publications used in office programs. \u2022 Serves with special projects or special events as required. \u2022 Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: \u2022 Excellent oral and written communication skills including attention to detail, impeccable grammar, ability to proofread \u2022 Basic computation and bookkeeping skills \u2022 Excellent computer skills, proficiency in MS Office with expertise in Word, Excel, Outlook \u2022 Excellent problem solving abilities \u2022 Ability to work independently \u2022 Ability to prioritize and perform multiple tasks simultaneously \u2022 Ability to take initiative and consistently meet deadlines \u2022 Ability to work closely and well with others \u2022 Ability to maintain confidentiality and discretion \u2022 Must possess a professional demeanor \u2022 Ability to demonstrate an attitude and behavior that reflects the values and mission of the department and University. Physical Demands and Working Conditions: 1. Work is primarily indoors, but requires the incumbent to be in an outdoor environment when traveling between campus buildings or off campus 2. Standard office hours are 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. but the schedule will be flexible to meet building security needs. Attendance at evening and weekend events may be required. 3. Off-campus travel is required and incumbent must possess the ability to travel locally. Incumbent must complete the university risk management driving course. 4. Incumbent will be exposed to frequent noise caused by telephones and office machines 5. Professional business attire is required. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c28a1e4a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Law School Law School Locations Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) 06e06f1e Last Name (required) 176cfb47 Email (required) 6f3e449b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Arts & Sciences The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health profession related programs. While area of specialization is open, candidates will be expected to teach Human Anatomy and Human Physiology. Additional courses may include Introductory Biology for Majors, Microbiology, and/or Immunology or other courses to complement the pre-health profession related curriculum. NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment Dance and Entertainment School Oklahoma City University invites applications for the nine-month, non-tenure track full-time faculty position of Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment beginning in January 2027 or August 2027. Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor) PA Program Oklahoma City University invites applications for the position of Principal Faculty, Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor in the Physician Assistant (PA) Program. This is a full-time, 12-month non-tenure track position located in the heart of Oklahoma City. The successful candidate will contribute to the education and development of future healthcare professionals and play a pivotal role in advancing the mission of the PA program. Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time or half-time adult-gerontology acute care nurse practitioner (AGACNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month or 12-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Administrative Assistant II Law School The Administrative Assistant II serves as the main point of contact for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the Law School by creating positive first and last impressions, as well as supporting the Law Dean's Office and law school departments. The Administrative Assistant II will work and communicate effectively with the judiciary, donors, alumni, attorneys, faculty, staff, students, vendors, and general public. While maintaining a pleasant and professional demeanor, this position will work with diverse, frequently changing priorities and situations. The Administrative Assistant II will demonstrate confidentiality, reliability, discretion, accuracy, and a strong service orientation. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 78d7fefb Last Name (required) 47a5707b Email (required) 45882af1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details \u00d7 This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/university-adjunct-nursing-undergraduate-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states-625cc8d9-6954-403e-9ecd-d4c1c89a04a5": {"title": "University Adjunct - Nursing - Undergraduate", "description": "University Adjunct - Nursing - Undergraduate - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States University Adjunct - Nursing - Undergraduate - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode University Adjunct - Nursing - Undergraduate Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Academic Affairs Adjunct Opening at: Sep 23 2026 - 16:00 CDT P Area: Nursing School Department: Nursing School FLSA Status: Exempt Benefit Eligibility: No Position Summary: The Kramer School of Nursing occasionally has openings for part-time temporary adjunct instructors teaching undergraduate courses. Applying for a part-time adjunct teaching appointment allows faculty chairs from across the School to access candidate materials if/when a teaching need arises throughout the current or future academic year. Learn more about undergraduate degree programs here . Duties and Responsibilities: Conduct formal classes Supervise student clinical experiences and communicate with preceptors and clinical staff Evaluate student learning, skills, and abilities and maintain records of such evaluations Serve the University and the Kramer School of Nursing, including volunteer options to serve on committees Retain clinical and/or role function excellence through continued education and practice Adhere to all policies within the Oklahoma City University Faculty Handbook, KSN Faculty Handbooks, the OCU Student Handbook, and the KSN Student Handbook. Participate in university activities and professional organizations as a member and a leader as desired Other duties as assigned. Support the integrity of curricula, encouraging student success, and promoting the mission of the Kramer School of Nursing and the university Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications: Bachelors of Science in Nursing (BSN) required Evidence of current practice with a minimum of two (2) years full time equivalent practice as a Registered Nurse in a clinical setting preceding the first date of first employment as a teacher Current, unencumbered license in the state of Oklahoma and/or a compact license Preferred Qualifications: Masters of Science in Nursing (MSN) Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Computer skills sufficient to deliver online instruction (if applicable), navigate course management software, and common Microsoft Office applications Flexible teaching style to accommodate individual learning styles Ability to maintain course schedule through regular, punctual attendance Additional Information: Working Conditions and Physical Demands: The work requirements for this position include teaching during daytime and some evening hours depending upon the needs of the department and its students. Most traditional classes are held in the Kramer School of Nursing building on the OCU campus. The online-only RN to BSN program is delivered remotely. For those who are assigned to teach remotely, the university currently supports residency in the following states only: Alabama, Arkansas, Colorado, Missouri, New Mexico, Oregon, and Virginia. Must be able to lift and carry equipment and supplies weighing up to 40 pounds. Must be able to bend, stoop, and reach. Manual dexterity to operate a computer keyboard and other business machines efficiently Near vision sufficient to read written communications and computer display screens Adequate hearing to communicate effectively in person and by phone Stamina to teach clinical practicum on site with timely access by students if assigned such duties Work is primarily indoors but requires the incumbent to be in an outdoor environment when traveling between campus buildings or off campus. Incumbents will be exposed to frequent noise caused by telephones and office machines. Access to a personal vehicle and ability to drive in a variety of locations (urban/rural) and travel up to four (4)-to-five (5) hours for in-person practicum visits Some assignments that take place in clinical facilities may involve potential exposure to factors typically present in health care institutions. Interested adjuncts must apply fully and online to be considered. Candidates who are selected and accept teaching assignments must provide their current CV and transcripts upon hire. All university employees must complete a criminal background check and mandatory training. Once hired, adjunct faculty are typically onboarded at least two weeks before the beginning of the semester to which they are assigned. Adjuncts who do not complete all steps in the hiring and onboarding process in a timely manner may experience a delay in pay. Please review the adjunct pay schedule here . About the Kramer School of Nursing at Oklahoma City University The Kramer School of Nursing first opened its doors on the Oklahoma City University campus in 1981. Named the No. 1 private nursing school in Oklahoma by Nursing Schools Almanac and recognized in the top 15 nursing schools in the southwest region, the school offers a range of undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs taught by faculty members who are experienced nurses, many of whom are doctorally prepared and/or Certified Nurse Educators. Dedicated staff and committed community leaders work in tandem to ensure the school is a learning environment that allows students to advance their careers. The school offers a Bachelor of Science in Nursing on campus and online, and an online Master of Science in Nursing. Registered nurses can also pursue an RN-BSN or RN-MSN. Students can earn post-master\u2019s certificates in Nursing Education and Leadership, Family Nurse Practitioner, Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner and Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner. Students may also earn a Family Nurse Practitioner, Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner and Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner through the BSN-DNP program. Also offered are post master\u2019s Doctor of Nursing Practice and Ph.D. degree programs. At Kramer, we foster a learning environment where students are challenged to think critically and holistically \u2013 encouraging them to use their passion and knowledge to advance the profession of nursing. From undergraduate students taking pre-nursing general education courses, to doctorate students working on cutting-edge research, Kramer School of Nursing has a host of opportunities for any level of nursing. About Oklahoma City University Oklahoma City University was founded in 1904 and is a coeducational, urban, private university located in the Uptown district of Oklahoma City. The university is affiliated with the United Methodist Church and offers a wide variety of degrees in the liberal arts and sciences disciplines. Oklahoma City University is the only Oklahoma institution listed in the top tier of the regional, master's-level university category by U.S. News and World Report magazine. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert cf3e91ff Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Nursing School Nursing School Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) 2e1fd2fe Last Name (required) 03153d5d Email (re