"Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges 12 Month Faculty Opening at: Sep 3 2026 - 09:00 CDT VP Area: Nursing School Department: Nursing School FLSA Status: Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: The Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator provides academic and administrative leadership for the Kramer School of Nursing and serves as the designated Nurse Administrator for purposes of ACEN accreditation and Oklahoma Board of Nursing program approval. Reporting directly to the Dean of the College of Nursing and Health Professions, the Senior Associate Dean holds the authority and accountability required of the Nurse Administrator under Oklahoma Board of Nursing rules, including direct responsibility for administration of the School\u2019s nursing education program, preparation and administration of the School budget, implementation of faculty development programs, and recommendation of qualified faculty for appointment, promotion, tenure (if applicable), and retention. The Senior Associate Dean ensures compliance and alignment with applicable accreditation and regulatory body standards and reporting requirements. As a senior member of college leadership, the Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator works collaboratively with the Dean in providing strategic and operational direction for the College. To learn more: Senior Associate Dean Nurse Administrator Prospectus (Aug 2026).pdf Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree required; degree must be in nursing, or a related field with a Master of Science in Nursing also held. Evidence of current practice with a minimum of five (5) years full-time equivalent practice as a Registered Nurse in a clinical setting, preceding the first date of employment as faculty per requirements of the Oklahoma Nursing Practice Act and Rules and Regulations of said Act. 485:10-5-3.2 (2024) Minimum of five (5) years teaching experience at the baccalaureate level or higher in nursing Demonstrated knowledge of nursing accreditation standards (ACEN or CCNE) and Oklahoma Board of Nursing requirements Hold a valid license to practice as a Registered Nurse in the State of Oklahoma (or receive licensure before start date) Preferred Qualifications: Academic administrative experience preferred Job Duties: Academic and Program Leadership Oversees the academic programs of the Kramer School of Nursing, ensuring compliance with requirements of the Board of Trustees, the President, and applicable accreditation bodies, and keeping the Dean informed of program status and significant developments. Supports continuous improvement of nursing education programs by contributing to the assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of School programs under the Dean's direction. Assures that adequate provisions are made to advise nursing students regarding their academic programs. Oversees the day-to-day quality of instruction and availability of academic resources. Teaches courses as assigned based on programmatic and operational needs. Retains nursing expertise through continued education and practice. Administrative and Operational Leadership Holds primary responsibility for preparation and administration of the KSN budget with faculty input; monitors expenditures and ensures fiscal operations align with the allocation framework established in coordination with the Dean. Supports the Dean in organizing the School to efficiently administer its academic and administrative programs and committees. Administers the Office of the Senior Associate Dean in a manner that fosters responsiveness to students, faculty, senior university management, and other university offices, in alignment with the Dean's direction. Directs faculty development and evaluation processes; makes recommendations to the Dean regarding promotion, tenure, and retention; and oversees faculty workload and overload policies consistent with accreditation standards and OBN requirements. Assists with schedule development and faculty teaching assignments, subject to Dean approval. Supports recruitment, hiring, and orientation of faculty and staff for the School in coordination with the Dean, assuring that qualifications meet professional accreditation standards. Monitors School faculty and staff capacity and brings workforce needs to the Dean's attention. Manages staff time records and leave requests as assigned. Coordinates financial aid awarded by the School as directed by the Dean and university policy. Accreditation and Compliance Serves as the designated Nurse Administrator and primary institutional authority on nursing accreditation, bringing specialized expertise in ACEN or CCNE standards. Leads all accreditation activities for the KSN, including self-study preparation, site visit coordination, and ongoing compliance with ACEN or CCNE standards and Oklahoma Board of Nursing approval requirements. Keeps the Dean informed of accreditation status, findings, and required actions, translating nursing-specific accreditation requirements into institutional context. Directs program assessment processes to ensure continuous quality improvement in alignment with accreditation standards. Responsible for notification to the Oklahoma Board of Nursing of faculty appointments, changes in the program or its administration, and reports as directed by the Board. Adheres to all policies within the Oklahoma City University Faculty Handbook and the KSN Employee Handbook. Strategic Planning and University Engagement Contributes to the strategic planning processes of the School and the College of Nursing and Health Professions under the Dean's leadership. Supports the School executive board and serves as a liaison between the School, the university, and the broader nursing community, as directed by the Dean. Maintains collaborative working relationships with other academic and administrative offices on campus on behalf of the School. Participates in university-wide activities and committees as appropriate or as directed by the Dean or university senior leadership. Serves as representative to nursing education and service organizations as designated by the Dean. External Relations and Scholarship Represents the School in local, state, national, and international settings through public speaking and other roles, as authorized by the Dean. Supports fundraising efforts for the School in coordination with and under the direction of the Dean. Participates in externally validated scholarly activities and professional organizations as both member and leader. Serves as a resource in areas of expertise to faculty, personnel, and the community. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to speak effectively before both large and small groups Ability to engage with diverse constituencies with multiple and competing interests Excellent writing skills, as demonstrated in professional work samples submitted with application materials Excellent interpersonal and oral communication skills Commitment to diversity among School personnel and a cross-cultural curriculum Proficiency in word processing, spreadsheet, and presentation software Excellent problem-solving, leadership, and management skills Ability to understand and balance both faculty and student perspectives Strong work ethic, personal integrity, and positive outlook on challenges Detail-oriented, organized, and punctual in managing work and personnel Commitment to upholding the mission of Oklahoma City University Physical Demands and Working Conditions: Constantly operates a computer and other office machinery. Constantly visually identifies, observes, and assesses. Frequently communicates with university constituents. Frequently remains in a stationary position (standing and/or sitting). Occasionally moves to accomplish tasks and/or to get from one worksite to another. Occasionally moves common office materials. The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations (in accordance with ADA requirements) may be made, upon request, to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is primarily indoors, with some travel between campus buildings or off campus Attendance at evening and weekend events may be required Off-campus, state, regional, and national travel may be required Exposure to frequent noise caused by telephones and office machines Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert fcd8a529 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Nursing School Nursing School Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) eaf675fd Last Name (required) 2e9f0997 Email (required) b33e17a2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Arts & Sciences The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health profession related programs. While area of specialization is open, candidates will be expected to teach Human Anatomy and Human Physiology. Additional courses may include Introductory Biology for Majors, Microbiology, and/or Immunology or other courses to complement the pre-health profession related curriculum. NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment Dance and Entertainment School Oklahoma City University invites applications for the nine-month, non-tenure track full-time faculty position of Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment beginning in January 2027 or August 2027. Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor) PA Program Oklahoma City University invites applications for the position of Principal Faculty, Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor in the Physician Assistant (PA) Program. This is a full-time, 12-month non-tenure track position located in the heart of Oklahoma City. The successful candidate will contribute to the education and development of future healthcare professionals and play a pivotal role in advancing the mission of the PA program. Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time or half-time adult-gerontology acute care nurse practitioner (AGACNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month or 12-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Administrative Assistant II Law School The Administrative Assistant II serves as the main point of contact for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the Law School by creating positive first and last impressions, as well as supporting the Law Dean's Office and law school departments. The Administrative Assistant II will work and communicate effectively with the judiciary, donors, alumni, attorneys, faculty, staff, students, vendors, and general public. While maintaining a pleasant and professional demeanor, this position will work with diverse, frequently changing priorities and situations. The Administrative Assistant II will demonstrate confidentiality, reliability, discretion, accuracy, and a strong service orientation. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 9b7288c8 Last Name (required) 30e1e2e7 Email (required) 0fc30b30 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details \u00d7 This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/program-director-law-school-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {"title": "Program Director", "description": "Program Director - Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Program Director - Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Program Director Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges 12 Month Faculty Opening at: Sep 2 2026 - 09:00 CDT VP Area: Law School Department: Law School FLSA Status: Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: OKLAHOMA CITY UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF LAW invites applications for the position of Program Director for the launch of its online J.D. program, which is currently being developed. The online J.D. program will be fully online, and courses are likely to be both asynchronous and synchronous. All online J.D. program faculty and staff will fulfill their responsibilities in person at OCU Law. The Program Director will provide strategic leadership and oversight for all academic and administrative aspects of the online J.D., ensuring compliance with ABA Standard 306 and related accreditation requirements. The Director is responsible for maintaining academic quality, curricular coherence, and measurable learning outcomes, thereby ensuring that the online J.D. maintains rigor and educational equivalence with the in-person J.D. program. Working collaboratively with faculty leadership, academic committees, instructional designers, and technology staff, the Director will promote innovation, evaluate program effectiveness, and advance strategic initiatives that support program growth, quality, and continuous improvement. The Director will oversee student success initiatives by monitoring academic progress, retention, completion, and other key performance metrics and by implementing data-informed interventions to improve outcomes. In collaboration with Student Services and other law school departments, the Director will ensure that online J.D. students have meaningful access to advising, academic support, career services, and integration with the broader law school community. The Director will also develop and analyze program data to guide decision-making, oversee the online J.D. budget, and supervise program staff to support the effective delivery and long-term success of the program. Candidates should have an excellent academic background and a commitment to effective online education, as well as to integrity and a welcoming environment. Candidates for a tenure or tenure-track position must have demonstrated potential as a scholar. Candidates must have a J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school or a foreign law degree with a U.S. LL.M. or S.J.D. OCU Law anticipates hiring 2-3 faculty members and a Legal Research and Writing Professor during the 2026-2027 hiring season, with successful candidates beginning appointments in fall 2027. Our beautiful, historic law building is in downtown Oklahoma City, the 21st-most-populous city in America, within walking distance of the federal and county courthouses. The Mayor of OKC, David Holt, is our OCU Law Dean. OCU Law is home to the Oklahoma Innocence Project, the Tribal Sovereignty Institute, and the USPTO\u2019s Regional Pro Bono Patent Program. To apply, please submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae through the University hiring portal: https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/search . Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. No final hiring decisions can be made until candidates have applied through this portal. For more information, contact the Chair of the Faculty Appointments Committee, Professor and Associate Dean Lee Peoples, at lpeoples@okcu.edu . Oklahoma City University is an equal opportunity employer and affirms the values and goals of diversity. See OCU Nondiscrimination Statement . Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert ac5cd465 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Law School Law School Locations Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) 872e8b44 Last Name (required) ea393252 Email (required) 76b0ce1b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Arts & Sciences The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health