d on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Administrative Assistant II Law School The Administrative Assistant II serves as the main point of contact for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the Law School by creating positive first and last impressions, as well as supporting the Law Dean's Office and law school departments. The Administrative Assistant II will work and communicate effectively with the judiciary, donors, alumni, attorneys, faculty, staff, students, vendors, and general public. While maintaining a pleasant and professional demeanor, this position will work with diverse, frequently changing priorities and situations. The Administrative Assistant II will demonstrate confidentiality, reliability, discretion, accuracy, and a strong service orientation. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 4e2fdcc0 Last Name (required) d341b2d8 Email (required) 87d6f9ab Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details \u00d7 This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/recruitment-specialist-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {"title": "Recruitment Specialist", "description": "Recruitment Specialist - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Recruitment Specialist - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Recruitment Specialist Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Administration Regular Full-Time Staff Opening at: Aug 31 2026 - 09:00 CDT VP Area: Human Resources Department: Human Resources FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: Full-Time | | $20.67 \u2013 $22.84/hour Oklahoma City University is seeking an organized, service-minded Recruitment Specialist to coordinate hiring across our campus community, from the first job posting to the new hire's first day. This role is ideal for an HR professional who thrives on process, is ready for ownership of a function, and understands that every search reflects the institution. What You'll Do Coordinate searches across all employment types, staff, faculty, adjunct, and contingent, from vacancy approval through offer acceptance Work with hiring managers to develop search strategies, build interview processes, and keep things moving Own and operate our applicant tracking system (PageUp), including training others and keeping data clean Be the point of contact candidates hear from first and count on through pre-boarding: offer, background check, I-9, and Banner record setup Train hiring managers on process and procedure so searches run consistently and every candidate is treated with respect, including the ones we don't hire Expand how we recruit: job fairs, sourcing strategies, employer brand, community partnerships Track what's working, flag what isn't, and bring ideas Contribute to the department's ongoing efforts to enhance employee engagement and recognition across the university community What You'll Bring 3+ years of progressive HR, talent acquisition, or related experience Strong organizational skills and genuine attention to detail Experience with applicant tracking systems or complex HR software A service orientation, responsive, organized, and welcoming whether you're talking to a finalist or a frustrated hiring manager The instinct to ask questions and the confidence to raise a concern when something doesn't seem right Associate's degree required; bachelor's preferred. Relevant experience may substitute year for year. PHR or SHRM-CP a plus, we'll support you in getting there. Higher education experience and PageUp or Banner familiarity are a bonus, not a requirement. Why You'll Want to Work Here You'll join a small, collaborative HR team that works closely with leaders and employees across the university to support great hires, smooth onboarding, and a positive employee experience. Health & Wellness Choice of medical plans with OCU covering 70% of employee premiums On-campus health clinic at no cost to plan members $0 telehealth for medical and behavioral health Dental, vision, prescription savings, and free campus fitness center access Weekly paid wellness time Time Off That Matters Generous PTO including vacation, sick leave, and ~16.5 paid holidays Summer schedule with Fridays off, full pay, four-day workweek Financial Security 403(b) retirement plan with up to 5% university match Employer-paid basic life insurance and long-term disability FSA and HSA options with university HSA matching Education & Campus Perks Tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents National tuition exchange program participation Free admission to athletic events, discounted arts performances and meals Employee Assistance Program Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 7cfb70e6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Human Resources Human Resources Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) 50c27657 Last Name (required) d16db881 Email (required) 37054c0a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Arts & Sciences The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health profession related programs. While area of specialization is open, candidates will be expected to teach Human Anatomy and Human Physiology. Additional courses may include Introductory Biology for Majors, Microbiology, and/or Immunology or other courses to complement the pre-health profession related curriculum. NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment Dance and Entertainment School Oklahoma City University invites applications for the nine-month, non-tenure track full-time faculty position of Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment beginning in January 2027 or August 2027. Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor) PA Program Oklahoma City University invites applications for the position of Principal Faculty, Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor in the Physician Assistant (PA) Program. This is a full-time, 12-month non-tenure track position located in the heart of Oklahoma City. The successful candidate will contribute to the education and development of future healthcare professionals and play a pivotal role in advancing the mission of the PA program. Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time or half-time adult-gerontology acute care nurse practitioner (AGACNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month or 12-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Administrative Assistant II Law School The Administrative Assistant II serves as the main point of contact for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the Law School by creating positive first and last impressions, as well as supporting the Law Dean's Office and law school departments. The Administrative Assistant II will work and communicate effectively with the judiciary, donors, alumni, attorneys, faculty, staff, students, vendors, and general public. While maintaining a pleasant and professional demeanor, this position will work with diverse, frequently changing priorities and situations. The Administrative Assistant II will demonstrate confidentiality, reliability, discretion, accuracy, and a strong service orientation. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 21971e5b Last Name (required) 6396dffa Email (required) 81138bd3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details \u00d7 This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/preventative-maintenance-program-specialist-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {"title": "Preventative Maintenance Program Specialist", "description": "Preventative Maintenance Program Specialist - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Preventative Maintenance Program Specialist - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Preventative Maintenance Program Specialist Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Facilities Regular Full-Time Staff Opening at: Sep 1 2026 - 09:00 CDT VP Area: Facilities Department: Facilities FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Hourly Rate: Up to $19.47 Position Summary: This position is responsible for the day-to-day maintenance operations of the HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and mechanical systems for the university. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum 3 years experience in commercial maintenance. Job Duties: Research proper maintenance practices for various equipment and implement these into our preventative maintenance program. Perform routine preventive maintenance to ensure that building systems operate efficiently and the physical condition of buildings does not deteriorate. Use equipment, instruments, and tools in accordance with departmental standards; return items to designated locations promptly upon completion of task or at the end of each shift. Diagnose mechanical problems and determine how to correct them, checking blueprints, repair manuals, and parts catalogs as necessary. Inspect, operate, and test machinery and equipment in order to diagnose machine malfunctions. Accurately and consistently record maintenance and repair work performed. Apply safety precaution pertaining to: Safety regulations and procedures; chemical safety, hazard communication program; personal protective equipment; lifting procedures, lock out/ tag out procedures, back injury prevention; flammable storage, housekeeping; fire extinguisher training. Perform other duties as assigned. - (Essential) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of machines and tools, including their designs, uses, repair, and maintenance. Knowledge of materials, methods, and the tools involved in the construction or repair of houses, buildings, or other structures. Equipment Maintenance- Performing routine maintenance on equipment and determining when and what kind of maintenance is needed. Repairing- Repairing machines or systems using the needed tools. Troubleshooting-Determining causes of operating errors and deciding what to do about it. Active Listening-Giving full attention to what other people are saying, taking time to understand the points being made, asking questions as appropriate, and not interrupting at inappropriate times. Equipment Selection-Determining the kind of tools and equipment needed to do a job. Reading Comprehension-Understanding written sentences and paragraphs in work related documents. Critical Thinking- Using logic and reasoning to identify the strengths and weaknesses of alternative solutions, conclusions or approaches to problems. Good computer skills. Physical Demands and Working Conditions: Primarily inside, occasionally outside, exposed to heat, cold, humidity, etc. Exposed to temperature changes of 20 degrees to 30 degrees or more when going from boiler room or chiller to another location. Possibility of injuries such as sprains, fractures, deep cuts, etc. when repairing systems and operating machinery and equipment such as welding torches, grinders, air hammers, table drills, pumps, motors, etc. Occasional work with ladders, scaffolding, platforms, etc., 12 feet or more above floor or ground level. Exposed to steady and fairly loud noises from machinery and equipment such as chillers, air conditioning units, boilers, and pumps. Exposed to large amounts of dust when performing tasks such as changing filters, operating grinding machine. Occasional to frequent exposure to chemical irritants such as cleaning solvents, chemicals used to balance the water. Subject to 24-hour emergency call, including weekends and holidays. Frequent local area travel to make repairs at different buildings and to pick up parts, etc. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d722906b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Facilities Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) d0da61cb Last Name (required) 93498c8b Email (required) a27a9bcf Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Arts & Sciences The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health profession related programs. While area of specialization is open, candidates will be expected to teach Human Anatomy and Human Physiology. Additional courses may include Introductory Biology for Majors, Microbiology, and/or Immunology or other courses to complement the pre-health profession related curriculum. NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need. Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment Dance and Entertainment School Oklahoma City University invites applications for the nine-month, non-tenure track full-time faculty position of Technical Director for Dance and Entertainment beginning in January 2027 or August 2027. Principal Faculty, Physician Assistant Program (Ass