se cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/carpenter-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {"title": "Carpenter", "description": "Carpenter - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Carpenter - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Carpenter Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Facilities Regular Full-Time Staff Opening at: Aug 25 2026 - 09:00 CDT VP Area: Facilities Department: Facilities FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Hourly rate: $18.54 Position Summary: The Carpenter/Maintenance Tech I is a member of the Facilities Department responsible for performing skilled carpentry work to build, repair, rebuild, remodel, and maintain campus building, facilities, and equipment in support of assigned projects. The Carpenter/Maintenance Tech I reports to the Assistant Director of Facilities and works closely with other members of the Facilities team. Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) years of skilled carpentry experience is required; or two (2) years of experience performing duties including skilled carpentry work; or equivalent combination of training, education, and experience that would provide the required knowledge and abilities and is required Job Duties: Demonstrates an attitude and behavior that reflects the values and mission of the department and University. Serves as a member of the dedicated Facilities Project Team dedicated to supporting projects and deferred maintenance. Performs skilled carpentry work in support of assigned projects and deferred maintenance orders. Examples of work may include: Remodels and repairs cabinets, counters, shelves, tables and miscellaneous furniture; Replaces and repairs door closures and locks Alters and repairs a variety of building structures such as walls, partitions, doorways, window frames, stairways and roofs Installs window glass and screens; applies wall and floor covering materials; installs ceramic and other types of tile Refinishes furniture and paints and stains building interiors and exteriors May occasionally make routine electrical, plumbing and mechanical repairs of building equipment Applies safety precaution pertaining to: safety regulations and procedures; chemical safety, hazard communication program; personal protective equipment; lifting procedures, back injury prevention; flammable storage, housekeeping; and fire extinguisher training. Participates in trainings, certifications, and other professional development and compliance activities as assigned. Performs other duties as assigned which could include associated Facilities department maintenance work as requested, including, but not limited to: snow removal, event set-up and clean-up, truck loading and unloading, etc. - (Essential) Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of tools and methods of the trade; applicable local building codes. Skilled in planning and completing carpentry projects. Knowledge of standard carpentry materials and supplies. Ability to read, interpret and work from blueprints; prepare rough sketches of work and estimates of material and labor; select proper materials to be used; work cooperatively with others; skillfully use the proper tools. Knowledge of and skill in operating, adjusting, and maintaining power operated carpentry tools and equipment on site and in a shop setting. Knowledge and skill in use of manually operated carpentry tools and equipment. Skill in the repair of damaged furniture, cabinets, walls, ceilings, doors, locks, etc. Physical Demands and Working Conditions: Frequent work on ladders and/or scaffolding. Possibility of working in confined spaces when working with ceiling structures. Frequent work near moving machinery and power tools. Exposed to pronounced strain or vibration when using power tools. Exposed to intermittent or continued loud and insistent noises caused by power equipment. Exposed to large amounts of dust in shops and on site. Possible exposure to chemical irritants such as contact cement, adhesives, and cleaning solutions. Subject to working near electrical equipment. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 9c64aa81 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Facilities Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) f6316915 Last Name (required) f33fcdbc Email (required) d32bd173 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology Arts & Sciences The Department of Biology in the Petree College of Arts and Sciences at Oklahoma City University is seeking tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Biology whose innovative and creative instruction will complement and enhance the department\u2019s pre-health profession related programs. While area of specialization is open, candidates will be expected to teach Human Anatomy and Human Physiology. Additional courses may include Introductory Biology for Majors, Microbiology, and/or Immunology or other courses to complement the pre-health profession related curriculum. NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor Nursing School Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner (PMHNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, ni